 ## tab-keys.mjs
 
-### §stable-tab-keys — closing a tab never renumbers the others
+### §contiguous-tab-keys — closing a tab renumbers the others
+- Since: 2026-10-22 (maintainer decision; supersedes §stable-tab-keys)
+- Decision: `closeTab` renumbers the remaining keys `t1, t2, t3, …` in order and resets `next` to `tabs.length + 1`,
+  so the URL never shows gaps (`?tabs=t1,t2`, not `?tabs=t1,t4,t7`).
+- Known cost: keys are still the React keys, so every tab to the right of a closed one gets a new key and remounts,
+  losing scroll position and unsaved form input — the failure behind §stable-tab-keys (incident 2026-08-29).
+- Evidence: `tab-keys.test.mjs` ("close renumbers keys", "open after close continues contiguously")
+
+### §stable-tab-keys — closing a tab never renumbers the others (superseded 2026-10-22 by §contiguous-tab-keys)
 - Since: 2026-09-02
 - Decision: a key is assigned once from `next` and is never reused or shifted. Closing a tab leaves a gap (`t1,t3`).
 - Forbidden: renumbering the remaining keys after a close to make them contiguous.
